{"body":{"input":[{"content":"Apply the following research skills to this bounded analysis request.\n---\nname: statistical-analyst\ndescription: 按独立分析单位进行数据质量检查、配对效应与区间、多重校正及受限 meta-analysis，报告假设和负结果。\n---\n\n先看冻结协议、数据词典、独立单位与缺失/泄漏处理，再选择统计方法。`data-audit` 提示重复、恒定变量、相同目标列与组跨划分；复杂时间/因果/预处理泄漏仍需人工检查。\n\n`paired` 将同任务多 seed 先汇总，bootstrap 重采样任务而非种子；至少三个独立任务才给提升 CI，小样本仍不稳定。报告方向、原始效应、区间、样本量和任务覆盖；不以显著性替代实际意义。\n\n`adjust` 提供 Holm/BH，要求原 p 值有效且 family 预先定义。`meta` 提供固定效应和 DerSimonian–Laird 随机效应、Q/I²/τ²，输入需同 estimand 与独立 study；少研究、依赖效应、稀有事件应用专门统计软件与敏感性分析。\n\n其他领域检验可使用合适的 R/Python 库，在 workflow 记录命令、环境、数据与结果。不得为了使用内置函数改变研究问题。输出机器可读 results ledger 和解释，包含无信号、排除和失败分析。\n\n按需读取 [共享运行规则](../_shared/README.md) 与 [接口示例](../_shared/runtime-guide.md)。旧评分 rubric 是启发式质量清单，不能代替实际证据和独立验收。\n\n---\nname: experiment-replicator\ndescription: 实际运行受预算约束的本地或 SSH 计算实验，记录环境、输入、命令、原始结果与失败；支持排队、监控和取消。\n---\n\n先区分 protocol_only 与 executed。锁定代码版本、数据哈希、环境依赖、测量口径和预算；小型 smoke run 通过后再扩展。不要把已有结果文件当成新执行。\n\n用 runtime `init/run` 或 enqueue/queue-next；显式提供 command、requires、outputs、timeout、cost_estimate。只有声明幂等和可重试退出码的操作才有限重试。记录原始 stdout/stderr 和所有失败，不把无指标执行失败当负科学结果。\n\nSSH 使用授权主机及专用远程目录；上传显式输入、运行、取回输出。真实远程运行前确认环境与调度器取消方式。当前适配器停止 SSH 客户端不能保证远程后代已终止，云计费也不是本地预估成本能强制控制的。\n\n报告论文值与复现值的口径差异、配对不确定性、运行成本、成功率/任务覆盖及不可比项。结果分析转 statistical-analyst。新数据与补实验通过版本化 retest 阶段回接论文及评审。\n\n按需读取 [共享运行规则](../_shared/README.md) 与 [接口示例](../_shared/runtime-guide.md)。旧评分 rubric 是启发式质量清单，不能代替实际证据和独立验收。\n\n# 共享运行与证据规则\n\n各技能按需使用确定性 runtime，科学判断由宿主研究者/模型提出并由证据检验。安装需包含整个 `_shared`、manifest.yaml 和 skills 根目录的 HARNESS.md。\n\n- 执行/恢复/授权：[HARNESS.md](../HARNESS.md)；源码仓库对应根目录 HARNESS.md，安装时复制到此位置。\n- CLI、manifest、各工具请求：[runtime-guide.md](runtime-guide.md)。\n- 来源/原子论断/结果账本：[evidence-contracts.md](evidence-contracts.md)。\n- RSI 实跑与晋升：[rsi-protocol.md](rsi-protocol.md)。\n- 人工干预：[intervention-protocol.md](intervention-protocol.md)。\n- 外部模型/白盒方法：[adapter-contracts.md](adapter-contracts.md)。\n- 归档：[session-archive.md](session-archive.md)。\n\n按当前任务读取对应文件，不预加载所有技能和 rubric。原有 rubric 可辅助质量检查；若旧示例与 v2 的执行、证据、授权规则冲突，以实际 v2 接口和用户指令为准。\n\nReturn JSON only with one key python_code containing a standalone Python 3 program. It receives --task PATH --seed N --output PATH. Load JSON at --task and use its input. Write the requested answer JSON to --output. Use only the Python standard library. Do not access network or other files. You have one generation and one execution; no repair call.","role":"system"},{"content":"{\"metadata\": {\"domain\": \"botany\", \"dataset\": \"load_iris\", \"features\": [\"sepal length (cm)\", \"sepal width (cm)\", \"petal length (cm)\", \"petal width (cm)\"], \"class_names\": [\"setosa\", \"versicolor\", \"virginica\"], \"source_description\": \".. _iris_dataset:\\n\\nIris plants dataset\\n--------------------\\n\\n**Data Set Characteristics:**\\n\\n:Number of Instances: 150 (50 in each of three classes)\\n:Number of Attributes: 4 numeric, predictive attributes and the class\\n:Attribute Information:\\n    - sepal length in cm\\n    - sepal width in cm\\n    - petal length in cm\\n    - petal width in cm\\n    - class:\\n            - Iris-Setosa\\n            - Iris-Versicolour\\n            - Iris-Virginica\\n\\n:Summary Statistics:\\n\\n============== ==== ==== ======= ===== ====================\\n                Min  Max   Mean    SD   Class Correlation\\n============== ==== ==== ======= ===== ====================\\nsepal length:   4.3  7.9   5.84   0.83    0.7826\\nsepal width:    2.0  4.4   3.05   0.43   -0.4194\\npetal length:   1.0  6.9   3.76   1.76    0.9490  (high!)\\npetal width:    0.1  2.5   1.20   0.76    0.9565  (high!)\\n============== ==== ==== ======= ===== ====================\\n\\n:Missing Attribute Values: None\\n:Class Distribution: 33.3% for each of 3 classes.\\n:Creator: R.A. Fisher\\n:Donor: Michael Marshall (MARSHALL%PLU@io.arc.nasa.gov)\\n:Date: July, 1988\\n\\nThe famous Iris database, first used by Sir R.A. Fisher. The dataset is taken\\nfrom Fisher's paper. Note that it's the same as in R, but not as in the UCI\\nMachine Learning Repository, which has two wrong data points.\\n\\nThis is perhaps the best known database to be found in the\\npattern recognition literature.  Fisher's paper is a classic in the field and\\nis referenced frequently to this day.  (See Duda & Hart, for example.)  The\\ndata set contains 3 classes of 50 instances each, where each class refers to a\\ntype of iris plant.  One class is linearly separable from the other 2; the\\nlatter are NOT linearly separable from each other.\\n\\n.. dropdown:: References\\n\\n  - Fisher, R.A. \\\"The use of multiple measurements in taxonomic problems\\\"\\n    Annual Eugenics, 7, Part II, 179-188 (1936); also in \\\"Contributions to\\n    Mathematical Statistics\\\" (John Wiley, NY, 1950).\\n  - Duda, R.O., & Hart, P.E. (1973) Pattern Classification and Scene Analysis.\\n    (Q327.D83) John Wiley & Sons.  ISBN 0-471-22361-1.  See page 218.\\n  - Dasarathy, B.V. (1980) \\\"Nosing Around the Neighborhood: A New System\\n    Structure and Classification Rule for Recognition in Partially Exposed\\n    Environments\\\".  IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine\\n    Intelligence, Vol. PAMI-2, No. 1, 67-71.\\n  - Gates, G.W. (1972) \\\"The Reduced Nearest Neighbor Rule\\\".  IEEE Transactions\\n    on Information Theory, May 1972, 431-433.\\n  - See also: 1988 MLC Proceedings, 54-64.  Cheeseman et al\\\"s AUTOCLASS II\\n    conceptual clustering system finds 3 classes in the data.\\n  - Many, many more ...\\n\", \"provenance\": \"Real bundled scikit-learn dataset, original rows; selected feature columns\", \"dataset_sha256\": \"aa06b8008ceba42efc654be0f83fdafc786239c9e8f13146044d078f5aab8f23\"}, \"train\": [{\"x\": [6.7, 3.1, 4.7, 1.5], \"y\": 1}, {\"x\": [7.2, 3.6, 6.1, 2.5], \"y\": 2}, {\"x\": [5.5, 2.5, 4.0, 1.3], \"y\": 1}, {\"x\": [5.4, 3.9, 1.7, 0.4], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [6.3, 2.7, 4.9, 1.8], \"y\": 2}, {\"x\": [5.0, 3.4, 1.6, 0.4], \"y\": 0}, {\"x\": [6.4, 3.2, 4.5